From: Custom Raumfeld firmware project
Subject: [PATCH] clk: si5351: enable fanout when selecting shared multisynth

The Connector 2 selects MS0 for CLK2. Setting CLK2_SRC alone leaves that
output without a clock unless MS_FANOUT_EN is also set. The vendor kernel
enabled this unconditionally; enable it when a shared source is selected.
RAM testing reproduced stalled McASP playback with register 187 bit 4 clear
and successful audible playback with it set, preserving all other bits.

Signed-off-by: Custom Raumfeld firmware project
---
 drivers/clk/clk-si5351.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-si5351.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-si5351.c
@@ -820,8 +820,12 @@
 		/* clk0/clk4 can only connect to its own multisync */
 		if (num == 0 || num == 4)
 			val = SI5351_CLK_INPUT_MULTISYNTH_N;
-		else
+		else {
 			val = SI5351_CLK_INPUT_MULTISYNTH_0_4;
+			/* Shared MS0/MS4 routing needs the fanout gate. */
+			si5351_set_bits(drvdata, SI5351_FANOUT_ENABLE,
+					SI5351_MULTISYNTH_ENABLE, SI5351_MULTISYNTH_ENABLE);
+		}
 		break;
 	case SI5351_CLKOUT_SRC_XTAL:
 		val = SI5351_CLK_INPUT_XTAL;
